          "note_id": "9TVKFP72JPo",
          "fields": {
            "display_title": "This is one of the early papers on the concept of using quantum qubits for neural network computations.  The authors propose a robust method to map data into entangled qubits; this method is efficient in the qubit space, which is an important consideration in quantum systems.  However, the actual optimization problem is not solved by the quantum computer, only the forward pass.  I see this as a start in a potentially new and important field.",
            "replying_to": "Replying to GenQu: A Hybrid System for Learning Classical Data in Quantum States"
          }
        },
